IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 8 ENFORCEMENT POWERS AND PROCEDURES: ss 78 to 83.  (ss 84 to 88 are in sgta-part8-penalties.l4.)
-- Seat: the person who is required to produce, examined, arrested or searched, or whose thing is seized; and the officer's power is
-- expressed as the conditions under which it may be exercised against that person.

§ `s 78 Power to require information, etc.`

-- src:5643 | 78.—(1) The Authority or any officer authorised by the Authority
-- src:5644 | in that behalf (called in this section the authorised officer) may, for
-- src:5645 | the purposes of conducting an investigation or for discharging the
-- src:5646 | Authority’s functions under this Act, by order require any person to
-- src:5647 | produce to the Authority any document, or to provide the Authority
-- src:5648 | with any information, which the Authority considers to be related to
-- src:5649 | any matter relevant to the investigation or for discharging its
-- src:5650 | functions under this Act.
@ref s 78(1) (src:5643-5650)
GIVEN `the person making the order is the Authority or an officer authorised by the Authority in that behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purposes of conducting an investigation or discharging the Authority's functions under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority considers the document or information to be related to a matter relevant to the investigation or to the discharge of its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(1): the Authority or the authorised officer may by order require the person to produce the document or provide the information` MEANS
    `the person making the order is the Authority or an officer authorised by the Authority in that behalf` AND `it is for the purposes of conducting an investigation or discharging the Authority's functions under the Act` AND `the Authority considers the document or information to be related to a matter relevant to the investigation or to the discharge of its functions`

-- src:5654 | (2) The Authority or the authorised officer is entitled without
-- src:5655 | payment to keep any copy or extract of any document furnished to the
-- src:5656 | Authority or the authorised officer under subsection (1).
@ref s 78(2) (src:5654-5656)
GIVEN `the document was furnished to the Authority or the authorised officer under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(2): the Authority or the authorised officer is entitled without payment to keep a copy or extract` MEANS
    `the document was furnished to the Authority or the authorised officer under subsection (1)`

-- src:5660 | (3) The Authority or the authorised officer has, at all reasonable
-- src:5661 | times in the day, full and free access to all buildings, places, books,
-- src:5662 | documents and other papers for the purpose of conducting an
-- src:5663 | investigation or discharging functions of the Authority under this Act,
-- src:5664 | and may, without payment, inspect, copy or make extracts from any
-- src:5665 | such books, documents or papers.
@ref s 78(3) (src:5660-5665)
GIVEN `it is at a reasonable time in the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of conducting an investigation or discharging functions of the Authority under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(3): the Authority or the authorised officer has full and free access to the building, place, book, document or other paper and may inspect, copy or make extracts without payment` MEANS
    `it is at a reasonable time in the day` AND `it is for the purpose of conducting an investigation or discharging functions of the Authority under the Act`

-- src:5672 | (4) The Authority may take possession of any equipment, books,
-- src:5673 | documents or papers where in its opinion —
-- src:5675 | (a) the equipment, books, documents or papers may be
-- src:5676 | interfered with or destroyed unless possession is taken; or
-- src:5678 | (b) the equipment, books, documents or papers may be
-- src:5679 | required as evidence in proceedings for an offence under
-- src:5680 | this Act or any regulations made under this Act.
@ref s 78(4) (src:5672-5680)
GIVEN `in the Authority's opinion the equipment, books, documents or papers may be interfered with or destroyed unless possession is taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the Authority's opinion the equipment, books, documents or papers may be required as evidence in proceedings for an offence under the Act or its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(4): the Authority may take possession of the equipment, books, documents or papers` MEANS
    `in the Authority's opinion the equipment, books, documents or papers may be interfered with or destroyed unless possession is taken` OR `in the Authority's opinion the equipment, books, documents or papers may be required as evidence in proceedings for an offence under the Act or its regulations`

-- src:5682 | (5) The rights conferred by this section include, in relation to
-- src:5683 | information recorded otherwise than in legible form, the right to
-- src:5684 | require the information to be made available in legible form for
-- src:5685 | inspection or for a copy or extract to be made of or from it.
@ref s 78(5) (src:5682-5685)
GIVEN `the information is recorded otherwise than in legible form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(5): the rights include requiring the information to be made available in legible form for inspection, or for a copy or extract` MEANS
    `the information is recorded otherwise than in legible form`

-- src:5687 | (6) The power under this section to require a person to produce a
-- src:5688 | document includes the power —
-- src:5690 | (a) if the document is produced, to require such person, or any
-- src:5691 | person who is a present or past officer of the person or is or
-- src:5692 | was at any time employed by the person, to provide an
-- src:5693 | explanation of the document; or
-- src:5695 | (b) if the document is not produced, to require such person to
-- src:5696 | state, to the best of the person’s knowledge and belief,
-- src:5697 | where it is.
-- src:5699 | [10/2005]
@ref s 78(6) (src:5687-5699)
GIVEN `the document is produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(6)(a): the Authority may require the person, or a present or past officer or employee of the person, to explain the document` MEANS
    `the document is produced`

GIVEN `the document is not produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(6)(b): the Authority may require the person to state, to the best of the person's knowledge and belief, where the document is` MEANS
    `the document is not produced`

-- src:5701 | (7) Any person who —
-- src:5703 | (a) fails to comply with any requirement specified in any order
-- src:5704 | under subsection (1);
-- src:5706 | (b) intentionally alters, suppresses or destroys any document
-- src:5707 | or information which the person has been required by any
-- src:5708 | order under subsection (1) to produce or provide; or
-- src:5710 | (c) in furnishing any information required of the person under
-- src:5711 | any order under subsection (1), makes any statement which
-- src:5712 | the person knows to be false in a material particular, or
-- src:5713 | recklessly makes any statement which is false in a material
-- src:5714 | particular,
-- src:5716 | shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 78(7) (src:5701-5716)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with a requirement specified in an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intentionally alters, suppresses or destroys a document or information the person was required to produce or provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, in furnishing information required, makes a statement the person knows to be false in a material particular, or recklessly makes one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(7): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person fails to comply with a requirement specified in an order under subsection (1)` OR `the person intentionally alters, suppresses or destroys a document or information the person was required to produce or provide` OR `the person, in furnishing information required, makes a statement the person knows to be false in a material particular, or recklessly makes one`

-- src:5723 | (8) If a person is charged with an offence under subsection (7) in
-- src:5724 | respect of a requirement to produce any document or provide any
-- src:5725 | information under subsection (1), it is a defence for the person to
-- src:5726 | prove that —
-- src:5728 | (a) the document was not in the possession or under the
-- src:5729 | control of the person;
-- src:5731 | (b) it was not reasonably practicable for the person to comply
-- src:5732 | with the requirement; or
-- src:5734 | (c) the person had a reasonable excuse for failing to provide
-- src:5735 | the information required.
@ref s 78(8) (src:5723-5735)
GIVEN `the person proves that the document was not in the possession or under the control of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that it was not reasonably practicable for the person to comply with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that the person had a reasonable excuse for failing to provide the information required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(8): the person charged has a defence to the offence under subsection (7) in respect of a requirement to produce or provide` MEANS
    `the person proves that the document was not in the possession or under the control of the person` OR `the person proves that it was not reasonably practicable for the person to comply with the requirement` OR `the person proves that the person had a reasonable excuse for failing to provide the information required`

-- src:5739 | (9) A person is not obliged under this section to disclose any
-- src:5740 | particulars as to which the person is under any statutory obligation to
-- src:5741 | observe secrecy.
@ref s 78(9) (src:5739-5741)
GIVEN `the person is under a statutory obligation to observe secrecy as to the particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(9): the person is obliged under this section to disclose the particulars` MEANS
    NOT `the person is under a statutory obligation to observe secrecy as to the particulars`

-- src:5743 | (10) In this section and sections 81 and 83 —
-- src:5745 | “document” includes any electronic record;
-- src:5747 | “electronic record” has the meaning given by the Electronic
-- src:5748 | Transactions Act 2010.
-- src:5750 | [59
@ref s 78(10) (src:5743-5750)
GIVEN `it includes an electronic record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(10): this is a "document"` MEANS
    `it is a document` OR `it includes an electronic record`

GIVEN `it has the meaning the Electronic Transactions Act 2010 gives electronic record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78(10): this is an "electronic record"` MEANS
    `it has the meaning the Electronic Transactions Act 2010 gives electronic record`

§ `s 79 Power to examine, etc.`

-- src:5756 | 79.—(1) An officer of the Authority who is authorised by the
-- src:5757 | Authority for the purpose of this section (called in this section the
-- src:5758 | authorised officer) may, for the purposes of investigating an offence
-- src:5759 | under this Act, do all or any of the following:
-- src:5761 | (a) require any person whom the authorised officer reasonably
-- src:5762 | believes to have committed that offence to furnish
-- src:5763 | evidence of that person’s identity;
-- src:5765 | (b) require, by written notice, any person within the limits of
-- src:5766 | Singapore, who appears to be acquainted with the facts or
-- src:5767 | circumstances of the matter to attend before the authorised
-- src:5768 | officer;
-- src:5770 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:5771 | 117 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:5773 | (c) examine orally any person who appears to be acquainted
-- src:5774 | with the facts or circumstances of the matter —
-- src:5776 | (i) whether before or after that person or anyone else is
-- src:5777 | charged with an offence in connection with the
-- src:5778 | matter; or
-- src:5780 | (ii) whether or not that person is to be called as a witness
-- src:5781 | in any inquiry, trial or other proceeding in connection
-- src:5782 | with the matter.
@ref s 79(1) (src:5756-5782)
GIVEN `the officer is an officer of the Authority authorised by the Authority for the purpose of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purposes of investigating an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer reasonably believes that the person has committed that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 79(1)(a): the authorised officer may require the person to furnish evidence of identity` MEANS
    `the officer is an officer of the Authority authorised by the Authority for the purpose of this section` AND `it is for the purposes of investigating an offence under the Act` AND `the officer reasonably believes that the person has committed that offence`

GIVEN `the officer is an officer of the Authority authorised by the Authority for the purpose of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purposes of investigating an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is within the limits of Singapore and appears to be acquainted with the facts or circumstances of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 79(1)(b) and (c): the authorised officer may require the person by written notice to attend before the officer, and may examine the person orally` MEANS
    `the officer is an officer of the Authority authorised by the Authority for the purpose of this section` AND `it is for the purposes of investigating an offence under the Act` AND `the person is within the limits of Singapore and appears to be acquainted with the facts or circumstances of the matter`

-- src:5786 | (2) A person examined under subsection (1)(c) is bound to state
-- src:5787 | truly what the person knows of the facts and circumstances of the
-- src:5788 | matter, except that the person need not say anything that might expose
-- src:5789 | the person to a criminal charge or punishment.
@ref s 79(2) (src:5786-5789)
GIVEN `the statement might expose the person to a criminal charge or punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 79(2): the person examined is bound to state it truly` MEANS
    NOT `the statement might expose the person to a criminal charge or punishment`

-- src:5793 | (3) A statement made by a person examined under subsection (1)(c)
-- src:5794 | must —
-- src:5796 | (a) be reduced to writing;
-- src:5798 | (b) be read over to the person;
-- src:5800 | (c) if the person does not understand English, be interpreted in
-- src:5801 | a language that the person understands; and
-- src:5803 | (d) after correction (if necessary), be signed by the person.
@ref s 79(3) (src:5793-5803)
GIVEN `the statement was reduced to writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was read over to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not understand English` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was interpreted in a language the person understands` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after correction, if necessary, it was signed by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 79(3): the statement was taken as the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the statement was reduced to writing`
    AND `it was read over to the person`
    AND ((NOT `the person does not understand English`) OR `it was interpreted in a language the person understands`)
    AND `after correction, if necessary, it was signed by the person`

-- src:5807 | (4) Any person who —
-- src:5809 | (a) without reasonable excuse, fails to furnish the information
-- src:5810 | required of that person under subsection (1)(a);
-- src:5812 | (b) without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with a notice
-- src:5813 | issued to that person under subsection (1)(b); or
-- src:5815 | (c) furnishes any information or makes any statement under
-- src:5816 | this section which the person knows to be false or
-- src:5817 | misleading in any material particular,
-- src:5819 | shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 79(4) (src:5807-5819)
GIVEN `the person, without reasonable excuse, fails to furnish the information required under subsection (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with a notice issued under subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person furnishes information or makes a statement under this section which the person knows to be false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 79(4): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person, without reasonable excuse, fails to furnish the information required under subsection (1)(a)` OR `the person, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with a notice issued under subsection (1)(b)` OR `the person furnishes information or makes a statement under this section which the person knows to be false or misleading in a material particular`

§ `ss 80 to 83: arrest, search, obstruction, costs`

-- src:5830 | 80.—(1) The Chief Executive or any employee of the Authority
-- src:5831 | deputed by the Chief Executive to act under this section or any police
-- src:5832 | officer may arrest without warrant —
-- src:5834 | (a) any person found committing or attempting to commit or
-- src:5835 | employing or aiding any person to commit a seizable
-- src:5836 | offence under this Act; or
-- src:5838 | (b) any person against whom a reasonable suspicion exists that
-- src:5839 | the person has been guilty of a seizable offence under this
-- src:5840 | Act,
-- src:5842 | and may search any person so arrested, except that a woman must not
-- src:5843 | be searched except by a woman.
@ref s 80(1) (src:5830-5843)
GIVEN `the person arresting is the Chief Executive, an employee of the Authority deputed by the Chief Executive to act under this section, or a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is found committing or attempting to commit, or employing or aiding another to commit, a seizable offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable suspicion exists that the person has been guilty of a seizable offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 80(1): the officer may arrest the person without warrant and search the person arrested` MEANS
    `the person arresting is the Chief Executive, an employee of the Authority deputed by the Chief Executive to act under this section, or a police officer` AND (`the person is found committing or attempting to commit, or employing or aiding another to commit, a seizable offence under the Act` OR `a reasonable suspicion exists that the person has been guilty of a seizable offence under the Act`)

GIVEN `the person to be searched is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the searcher is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 80(1): the search may be conducted by this searcher` MEANS
    (NOT `the person to be searched is a woman`) OR `the searcher is a woman`

-- src:5845 | (2) Every person so arrested must, together with any article as to
-- src:5846 | which an offence may have been committed or attempted to be
-- src:5847 | committed, be taken to a police station.
-- src:5849 | (3) For the purposes of this section, offences punishable under
-- src:5850 | sections 53, 61, 62, 63, 64, 65, 68 and 71 are deemed to be seizable
-- src:5851 | offences within the meaning of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010.
@ref s 80(2) and (3) (src:5845-5851)
GIVEN `the person was arrested under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 80(2): the person must be taken to a police station together with any article as to which an offence may have been committed or attempted` MEANS
    `the person was arrested under this section`

GIVEN `section of the offence` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 80(3): the offence is deemed to be a seizable offence within the meaning of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` MEANS
    elem `section of the offence` (LIST "53", "61", "62", "63", "64", "65", "68", "71")

-- src:5860 | 81.—(1) Whenever it appears to any police officer or the Chief
-- src:5861 | Executive or any employee of the Authority authorised to act for the
-- src:5862 | Chief Executive under this section that an offence under section 53 or
-- src:5863 | 64 is being committed or is about to be committed or attempted, or
-- src:5864 | that any article is concealed or deposited or contained in or on any
-- src:5865 | vessel, aircraft, vehicle or premises in contravention of either of those
-- src:5866 | sections, the police officer or the Chief Executive or the employee of
-- src:5867 | the Authority may, if he or she has reasonable grounds for believing
-- src:5868 | that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the article is
-- src:5869 | likely to be removed —
-- src:5871 | (a) stop and examine the vessel, aircraft or vehicle or enter the
-- src:5872 | premises and there search for and take possession of any
-- src:5874 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:5875 | 119 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:5877 | article and of any book or document which is reasonably
-- src:5878 | believed to have a bearing on the case; and
-- src:5880 | (b) arrest any person being in the vessel, aircraft, vehicle or
-- src:5881 | premises in whose possession the article may be found or
-- src:5882 | whom the police officer or the Chief Executive or the
-- src:5883 | employee of the Authority may reasonably suspect to have
-- src:5884 | concealed or deposited the article and may search any
-- src:5885 | person so arrested, except that a woman must not be
-- src:5886 | searched except by a woman.
@ref s 81(1) (src:5860-5886)
GIVEN `the officer is a police officer, the Chief Executive, or an employee of the Authority authorised to act for the Chief Executive under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears that an offence under section 53 or 64 is being committed, is about to be committed or attempted, or that an article is concealed, deposited or contained in or on a vessel, aircraft, vehicle or premises in contravention of either section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the article is likely to be removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(1)(a): the officer may stop and examine the vessel, aircraft or vehicle or enter the premises, and search for and take possession of the article and any book or document reasonably believed to have a bearing on the case` MEANS
    `the officer is a police officer, the Chief Executive, or an employee of the Authority authorised to act for the Chief Executive under this section` AND `it appears that an offence under section 53 or 64 is being committed, is about to be committed or attempted, or that an article is concealed, deposited or contained in or on a vessel, aircraft, vehicle or premises in contravention of either section` AND `the officer has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the article is likely to be removed`

GIVEN `the officer has the power under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in the vessel, aircraft, vehicle or premises and the article may be found in the person's possession, or the officer may reasonably suspect the person to have concealed or deposited the article` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(1)(b): the officer may arrest the person and search the person arrested (a woman only by a woman)` MEANS
    `the officer has the power under subsection (1)` AND `the person is in the vessel, aircraft, vehicle or premises and the article may be found in the person's possession, or the officer may reasonably suspect the person to have concealed or deposited the article`

-- src:5888 | (2) Every person so arrested must, together with any such article, be
-- src:5889 | taken to a police station.
@ref s 81(2) (src:5888-5889)
GIVEN `the person was arrested under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(2): the person must be taken to a police station together with the article` MEANS
    `the person was arrested under subsection (1)`

-- src:5896 | 82. Any person who intentionally obstructs a police officer or the
-- src:5897 | Chief Executive or any employee of the Authority authorised to act
-- src:5898 | for the Chief Executive in the execution of his or her duty under
-- src:5899 | section 57 or 81 shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 82 (src:5896-5899)
GIVEN `the person intentionally obstructs a police officer, the Chief Executive, or an employee of the Authority authorised to act for the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer or employee was in the execution of the duty under section 57 or 81` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 82: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person intentionally obstructs a police officer, the Chief Executive, or an employee of the Authority authorised to act for the Chief Executive` AND `the officer or employee was in the execution of the duty under section 57 or 81`

-- src:5907 | 83. In any proceedings before any court in respect of any
-- src:5908 | equipment, article, book or document seized in the exercise or the
-- src:5909 | purported exercise of any power conferred under this Act, a person is
-- src:5910 | not entitled to the costs of the proceedings or to any damages or other
-- src:5911 | relief other than an order for the return of the equipment, article, book
-- src:5912 | or document or the payment of their value unless the seizure was
-- src:5913 | made without reasonable or probable cause.
@ref s 83 (src:5907-5913)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of equipment, an article, a book or a document seized in the exercise or purported exercise of a power under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seizure was made without reasonable or probable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 83: the person is entitled to the costs of the proceedings or to damages or other relief beyond the return of the thing or payment of its value` MEANS
    `the proceedings are in respect of equipment, an article, a book or a document seized in the exercise or purported exercise of a power under the Act` AND `the seizure was made without reasonable or probable cause`
